                                                "sense_id": "3f96caa5-4f6e-3b79-b76a-446f7928be80",
                                                "text": "By “fight back,” he meant, basically, tweeting. Internet activism is sometimes derided as “slacktivism”—a fair characterization when an online campaign tries to, say, cure aids or end child labor."
                                            }
